00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.200
In this video, we’re gonna be going over
a couple of reasons why you absolutely should

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.880
NOT buy the new Galaxy Note 10 that Samsung
just revealed at their unpacked event.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.320
Now there’s also the Note 10+, which looks
to be a much better phone, but as we’ll

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:25.240
talk about in a minute, you should probably
think twice about buying that model as well!

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.740
We just finished the Note 10 event, and we
noticed that Samsung talked about a lot of

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:32.170
features that are already available on their
S10 line of phones.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:37.090
For example, the S10 already has the same
exact Dynamic AMOLED Display, except that

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:43.320
it’s actually 1440p instead of only 1080p
on the Note 10, which is a shocker!

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:47.750
The S10 already has the ultrasonic fingerprint
sensor that they showed off.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.820
It also seems to have the same exact cameras
as the Note 10.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:56.070
Samsung didn’t mention any camera differences
at all, except for the Live Focus video feature,

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:00.740
which seems to be only coming on the Note
10+, since it has the 3D Depth sensor.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:04.370
The Note 10 actually still has the same exact
processor as the S10.

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:10.750
Their spec sheets shows that the Note 10 has
the SM8150 7nm processor, but that’s actually

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:15.270
the codename for the Snapdragon 855 that’s
already in the S10.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:16.320
So there’s no difference there.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.320
They touted the vapor chamber on the new Note
10, but the S10 already has that.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:21.970
They mentioned support for Fast Wireless charging
2.0, and yep, the S10 has that as well.

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:26.310
And basically everything else they showed
off was either already available on the S10,

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:31.470
or a software feature, like Samsung Dex, which
is yet again, available on the S10.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:35.750
They did mention continuity between the Note
10 and Windows computers, which I think is

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:39.000
really cool, but that’s also coming to the
S10 as well.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.100
I’d say the biggest difference is the S-Pen,
which has gotten some pretty impressive updates,

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:48.800
